>fe'oca'emi'e tricrfraksizeicecmu .iji'a ca'emi'e .aclin.

Does 'tricrfraksizeicecmu' work as one word? I suspect it would fall
apart - if it falls apart at the 'zei' that's not really a problem,
because 'tricrfraksi zei cecmu' is valid and equally meaningful (though
cecmu != kampu); but I can't work out if it mightn't fall apart
somewhere else.

On another point, I would prefer tricrfraksinu to tricrfraksi. There's
no rule about how to do this, but IMHO arbitrarily docking a syllable
off the word is naughty.

